Reasoning on a Budget: Reproducing DeepSeek R1 with SFT + GRPO on AWS (Qwen2.5B) TL;DR: Fine-tune an instruction-tuned LLM (Qwen2.5B) on reasoning tasks using a DeepSeek R1-inspired pipeline (SFT + GRPO). Achieve competitive alignment using rule-based rewards — all for under $100 on AWS SageMaker. 📖 Read the Full Article (Narimissa, 2025) Reasoning on a Budget: Miniaturizing DeepSeek R1 with SFT-GRPO Alignment for Instruction-Tuned LLMs 📌 DOI: 10.36227/techrxiv.174742969.91776650/v1 The article provides: - Theoretical background and motivation - Full details of the SFT and GRPO training stages - Reward function design and prompting conventions - Experimental results and analysis - Discussion of limitations and future work We recommend starting with the article for a comprehensive understanding of the codebase, design decisions, and how to reproduce or build upon our results. ---
---
The trained model (after SFT and GRPO) is available on Hugging Face Hub: Essi-Narim/qwen2.5b-sft-grpo-reasoning You can load the model directly with Hugging Face Transformers: --- This project implements a modular DeepSeek R1-style training pipeline for reasoning-centric language models, using Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT) and Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO). The pipeline is designed for both local development (VS Code, Jupyter) and scalable training on AWS SageMaker. ---
